<p>![world map diagram with the unlock order, from New Zealand to Mexico](TODO: image:release-time-step-1 — diagram, our own art: a world map with numbered arrows showing the order 1 New Zealand to 14 Mexico)
<em>Caption: Diagram. The game unlocks time zone by time zone, starting in New Zealand.</em></p>
<p><strong>Unlocks in order:</strong> New Zealand → Australia → Japan and South Korea → Singapore and Hong Kong → India → Eastern Europe → <strong>central Europe (00:00 CET)</strong> → UK → Brazil → US East Coast (and, as observed, all of the US) → Mexico and Central America. The whole rollout takes about 19 hours, from 11:00 UTC Wednesday to 06:00 UTC Thursday.</p>
<p><strong>What the ✅ rows rest on:</strong> regional PlayStation Store listings tracked by <a href="https://www.gta6everything.com/unlock-times" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GTA 6 Everything</a> (63 countries, with Xbox Store cross-checks for 40), Push Square’s and GamesRadar’s New Zealand-trick conversions (NZ midnight = 11 AM GMT / 12 PM CET / 10 PM AEDT / 8 PM JST / 7 PM AWST), PC Gamer’s offset table, and Rockstar’s and PlayStation’s “midnight local time” wording.</p>
<p><strong>The 🔶 rows (US time zones, Brisbane, Perth):</strong> Rockstar’s wording says midnight <em>local</em> time everywhere, which would mean US Central 12:00 AM (07:00 CET), Mountain 12:00 AM (08:00 CET) and Pacific 12:00 AM (09:00 CET). However, PC Gamer and GamesRadar say US PlayStation unlock screens show <strong>one Eastern-time moment for the whole US</strong> (midnight ET = 11 PM Central, 10 PM Mountain, 9 PM Pacific), and PC Gamer says the same may be true on Xbox. Store data lists a single time per country, and Australia’s is the Sydney (AEDT) time, so Brisbane and Perth may be grouped the same way: the table shows that case (Brisbane 11 PM, Perth 9 PM on 18 Nov), but it is <strong>unconfirmed</strong>. Use the countdown on your own console and store page as the final word.</p>
<p><strong>Slovenia and Croatia:</strong> neither is named in the sources we found. Both sit in CET, and the German, Austrian and Italian store listings show 00:00 CET, so 00:00 CET is expected. Confirm on your console’s countdown.</p>
<p>The PT, ET, BRT, UK, CET, EET, IST, JST, AEDT and NZDT zones requested most often are all in the table above.</p>
<h3 id="how-to-see-your-own-countdown-do-this-first" tabindex="-1">How to see your own countdown (do this first)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>PS5:</strong> go to the home screen and open your <strong>Game Library</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong>. It shows as locked until your unlock time. If it shows a countdown, that countdown is the real time for your account.</li>
<li><strong>Xbox Series X|S:</strong> press the <strong>Xbox button</strong>, then go to <strong>My games &amp; apps</strong> and select <strong>Full library</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong> and check the release time on its page.</li>
<li>Compare it with the table above. If they differ, trust your console.</li>
</ol>
