<p>The Rockstar Support article itself could not be opened for this page, so its wording is taken from PlayStation’s support page and from outlets quoting it. We will re-check it after launch.</p>
<h2 id="platforms" tabindex="-1">Platforms</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>PS5 and PS5 Pro</strong>: native. <strong>Xbox Series X and Series S</strong>: native. (Rockstar, PlayStation, Xbox Wire)</li>
<li><strong>Xbox One</strong>: cloud streaming only through Xbox Cloud Gaming, starting <strong>1 AM ET on 19 November</strong>, using Xbox Series S graphics settings. (Xbox Wire)</li>
<li><strong>PS4</strong>: not playable. <strong>PC</strong>: no version announced on any official page we checked.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="preload-info" tabindex="-1">Preload info</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>PlayStation 5:</strong> preload opened at midnight local time on <strong>10 November 2026</strong> for digital pre-orders. (PlayStation support)</li>
<li><strong>Xbox Series X|S:</strong> preload opened at <strong>midnight GMT on 10 November</strong>. (USA Today, citing Rockstar’s announcement)</li>
<li><strong>Code-in-box (physical):</strong> the box holds a download code, with no disc. Redeem it to start preloading. Boxed copies were slated for retail from <strong>12 November</strong>. (Take-Two press release, PlayStation support)</li>
<li><strong>Size:</strong> PlayStation tells players to clear <strong>at least 212 GB</strong> on PS5. Rockstar’s figure is “up to 212 GB depending on console.” (PlayStation, USA Today)</li>
<li>Preloading does <strong>not</strong> unlock the game early. It only means you can press play the second your region hits midnight.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="launch-day-checklist" tabindex="-1">Launch-day checklist</h2>
<ol>
<li>Confirm the preload is 100% complete in your console’s downloads list (on PS5: Downloads/Uploads).</li>
<li>Keep the console on the account that bought the game.</li>
<li>Turn on Auto-Install and Stay Connected to the Internet in Rest Mode if you want your console to finish updates on its own (PlayStation support steps).</li>
<li>Install any day-one update before the unlock moment if one is offered. Its size has not been announced.</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="faq" tabindex="-1">FAQ</h2>
<h3 id="what-time-does-gta-6-unlock-in-the-us" tabindex="-1">What time does GTA 6 unlock in the US?</h3>
<p>At midnight Eastern Time on Thursday 19 November, which is 9:00 PM Pacific on Wednesday 18 November, based on US PlayStation unlock screens seen by GamesRadar and PC Gamer.</p>
<h3 id="what-time-does-gta-6-release-in-the-uk-and-europe" tabindex="-1">What time does GTA 6 release in the UK and Europe?</h3>
<p>Midnight local time: 00:00 GMT in the UK and 00:00 CET in central Europe (including Slovenia), both on Thursday 19 November.</p>
<h3 id="does-gta-6-unlock-at-06-00-cet" tabindex="-1">Does GTA 6 unlock at 06:00 CET?</h3>
<p>No. 06:00 CET is the US Eastern unlock. Central Europe unlocks at 00:00 CET.</p>
<h3 id="which-country-gets-gta-6-first" tabindex="-1">Which country gets GTA 6 first?</h3>
<p>New Zealand, at 12:00 AM NZDT on 19 November (11:00 UTC on 18 November).</p>
<h3 id="can-i-play-gta-6-early-by-preloading" tabindex="-1">Can I play GTA 6 early by preloading?</h3>
<p>No. Preloading only downloads the game. It stays locked until your region’s launch time.</p>
<h3 id="is-gta-6-coming-to-pc" tabindex="-1">Is GTA 6 coming to PC?</h3>
<p>No PC version has been announced on any official page we checked. The game is listed for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S.</p>
<h3 id="how-big-is-the-gta-6-download" tabindex="-1">How big is the GTA 6 download?</h3>
<p>Up to 212 GB depending on console. PlayStation recommends clearing at least 212 GB.</p>
